  "structure": {
    "block_count": 41,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Is It Safe to Use a Laptop While You're Pregnant?",
        "text_sha256": "f9fb2945bac79705cde215322db3ebc160fcfbd46a93625ed039277c5ed88940",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "by Heidi Murkoff , author of What to Expect When You're Expecting.",
        "text_sha256": "fe0f379871761f84993fc97638e1be60dfaee98ef922ce30fb241d275bfed786",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Updates to copy, sources, and formatting.",
        "text_sha256": "2bf448333081ffc8549a45a6c4b7fc711ee4b93575f0fffd3c4a6212c13581c2",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Ask Heidi Murkoff",
        "text_sha256": "ac7d5d65ef8df9ec0a9d8053a467eff02d16dae53d1cbcba802e080bfc2dd938",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I recently read that laptop use may hurt a man's fertility. Now I'm wondering if using a laptop might hurt my baby.\"",
        "text_sha256": "b8d38736d485451e4a44d38c94eb36c7e7e2f59fbbf7ace51311a487e0451644",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Balancing a laptop on your increasingly shrinking lap isn't easy — but it hasn't proven to be dangerous either. Although a few studies have shown a link between the heat emitted from a laptop and a decrease in a man's fertility, most experts agree that such low levels of heat don't pose a risk to a developing fetus.",
        "text_sha256": "ce77ebf50f5a1a1296f1a81c0b10e82219b1eddb359e09ca20ada78e47985ad3",
        "word_count": 58
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Neither is there a known radiation risk to your baby from using a computer or a laptop.",
        "text_sha256": "a9c25fcd852a9376906dc16913fd4bac3d69aa22f5941e6a49612e5cebb14937",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "cc3f7f0f4513969e418b56fb93ec0876fd96dd6498395b04301f70dbddff8a45",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Laptops are safe. Experts say the heat and radiation from this device won't affect your baby-on-board.",
        "text_sha256": "13dfc1ce8b22aa3e18b892e7313cf2f01cf7831214d258ecdf95d458f96a2d07",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Sit up straight! Hunching over a laptop on your growing belly can lead to an achy back. Your best bet: Place it on a table or desk for maximum comfort.",
        "text_sha256": "651074bb728622906186ef7dbacb9ef76aa6b6c2bc57fc80e63e50e086cde216",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Do what feels best. It's perfectly fine to be extra careful and skip resting your laptop on your belly (peace of mind = priceless).",
        "text_sha256": "845cf8762118e69bebf6fb665fdcf792bcadf69a5157cf5f6ddbcb79a4bbbabb",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "But to play it safe, you might want to keep the laptop away from your lap and off your belly — which would be a tough balancing act anyway.",
        "text_sha256": "60e040789cc9ee27f1ca82f2e0cb7744e7d1a8efd171c0a5b836f5edbe34ed0a",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "After all, the computer isn't called a bellytop. Besides, by perching your laptop on a desk or table during your pregnancy, you'll probably end up with less back strain — and fewer typos too.",
        "text_sha256": "e32dd691371d77929123b284a52540dfe3fa923efc4ceb62b3a847391a01b0f1",
        "word_count": 34
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "We've got more safety tips on the What to Expect app , plus expert guidance and trusted advice for every stage of your pregnancy.",
        "text_sha256": "b3fae614905367ba9a5e6d50e3a8c2b109f40eae28edbdc7c6f910be03418a57",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The bottom line? You're safe to keep typing away on your laptop while you're pregnant, so take that off your \"to-worry-about\" list. Using a laptop won't hurt your growing baby.",
        "text_sha256": "e064b0d88a4912de311bcab65e29e0b0e92e2881e187459ac4efe5a34a07ab71",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Don't work too hard,",
        "text_sha256": "b5690dbf2aa4ba259f49b460ed55387df7df9ca450fc3dfbe0d3150a2a9ab006",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Heidi Murkoff",
        "text_sha256": "6f05d1b1394d028842497499fff96bffb14810fb4a10d1a23a1ef1b82a72292e",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "blockquote",
        "tag": "blockquote",
        "text": "What to Expect When You're Expecting , 5th edition, Heidi Murkoff. WhatToExpect.com, Are Cellphones Safe During Pregnancy? Here’s What the Science Says , November 2025. National Institutes of Health, National Library of Medicine, Exposure to Electromagnetic Fields From Laptop Use of \"Laptop\" Computers , 2012. National Cancer Institute, Electromagnetic Fields and Cancer , May 2022. National Institutes of Health, National Library of Medicine, The Fundamental Reasons Why Laptop Computers Should Not Be Used on Your Lap , December 2016.",
        "text_sha256": "7e21666858d86998bde85231c91671c8b597f93cfc7d7891fd9182b6049a8cb0",
        "word_count": 79
      },
